## Summary

Implements the reproducible consolidated-calculation slice of #94 on top of merged #106.

- bills monthly plans and recurring add-ons for the upcoming calendar month;
- creates a one-time closed-month catch-up charge when an existing monthly plan or recurring add-on first moves from arrears billing to advance billing;
- bills ticket fees and usage from the closed period in arrears;
- adds first-period proration for plans and recurring add-ons that begin between calendar boundaries;
- bills annual plans only when their upcoming renewal period begins, skips terms ending at or before renewal, and prorates terms ending during the billed year;
- keeps one-time add-ons tied to their activation period;
- normalizes calendar period ends and gives every fixed-charge line a deterministic source reference so it cannot be billed twice;
- atomically claims included `UsageRecord` rows through the finalized invoice;
- preserves historical usage records if their event is deleted;
- continues to atomically claim platform-fee ledger entries;
- records the source amount, conversion rate, converted amount, and ECB rate date when currency conversion is used;
- aborts invoice generation when a required conversion rate is unavailable or invalid instead of finalizing an incomplete invoice.

Migration `0020` adds the nullable, protected invoice claim on `UsageRecord`. Migration `0021` preserves usage history by setting a deleted event reference to null. Existing usage records remain unclaimed and available to the first applicable billing run.

## Billing result

For the first run after the calculation transition, a consolidated invoice can contain:

- the closed month's plan and recurring add-on catch-up charge when that service period was not previously claimed;
- the upcoming month's plan and recurring add-ons in advance;
- a prorated closed-month plan/add-on line when service began during that month;
- closed-month ticket fees, usage, and overages in arrears;
- one-time add-ons activated during the closed month.

Subsequent runs recognize the preceding advance charge and do not bill that service period again. Repeated generation returns the existing invoice, fixed source keys cannot be reused, and claimed ledger/usage rows cannot enter another invoice.

## Phase boundary

This PR calculates and finalizes the Eventyay invoice. It does not create a Stripe PaymentIntent or collect money.

The next PR will add idempotent off-session Stripe collection for a finalized positive total, verified webhook state transitions, failure/action-required handling, and a zero-total no-payment path.

